      "writtenOn": "2018-04-24T22:02:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I added a comment that states which fields are valid for which return codes. You can use that if you decided on going with checking the return codes. This shouldn\u0027t be a problem if we setup a way for you to include pinweaver_types.h directly.\n\nOtherwise, the following logic to determine which fields are valid:\n\n1) Test if seconds_to_wait is zero. If it is not, seconds_to_wait is the only valid field. Otherwise, the unimported_leaf_data field is valid.\n\n2) Test if the number of attempts in the public section of the leaf data is zero. If it is, the high_entropy_secret field is valid. Otherwise, it is not valid.\n\nOn the trunks side I have been just copying the fields, but I will change it so the metadata and secret are zero length if they are not valid.",
